### Blocker 2: `stop()` cancellation is bypassed for a queued message when cancelled during `MessageTurn::after_message` yield
In [`run_actor`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L700-L741), the post-handler cancellation check ([line 731](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L731-L733)) runs **before** `turn.after_message(rx.is_empty()).await` ([line 736](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L735-L737)), and at the top of the next loop iteration `futures::future::select(recv, cancel)` ([line 715](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L715)) always polls `recv` **before** `cancel`.
- **Concrete Interleaving:**
  1. Actor $A$ on `spawned-shard-0` has $M_1, M_2$ queued in `rx`.
  2. Actor $A$ completes $M_1$. At [line 731](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L731), `cancellation_token.is_cancelled()` is `false`.
  3. At [line 736](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L736), `turn.after_message(false).await` calls `yield_now().await` and yields control of `spawned-shard-0`.
  4. Before Actor $A$ is re-polled, another task on `spawned-shard-0` (or another thread) calls `actor_a.child_handle().stop()`, cancelling `cancellation_token`.
  5. Actor $A$ resumes from `yield_now().await` and loops to [line 715](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L715): `future::select(recv, cancel).await`.
  6. `future::select` polls its first argument (`recv`) first. Because $M_2$ is already in `rx`, `rx.poll_recv(cx)` returns `Poll::Ready(Some(M_2))` without polling `cancel`.
  7. Actor $A$ executes $M_2$ after `stop()` was already issued, violating the contract tested by [`stop_finishes_in_flight_handler_and_rejects_queued_work`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/full_actor_shards.rs#L123-L152).

