## 4. Documented Tradeoffs, Deadlock Characteristics & Benchmark Caveats

- **Self-join / cyclic request deadlocks (inherent to sequential actor model):**
  - Calling `ctx.actor_ref().join().await` or `wait_exit().await` inside `started()`, `handle()`, or `stopped()` deadlocks indefinitely because [`completion_tx.send(Some(reason))`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L588) only runs after `run_actor` returns.
  - Self-requests (`ctx.request(...).await`) or cyclic requests ($A \leftrightarrow B$, whether on the same shard or across shards) deadlock until `DEFAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT` (5s).
  - Non-cyclic requests between two actors on the *same* shard ($A \to B$) do not deadlock because `A`'s `request` yields `Poll::Pending` to the shard's `current_thread` executor, which then polls `B` (and the shard's `rx.recv()` ingress task).
- **Sync blocking / `rt::block_on` on a shard worker:**
  - Calling [`rt::block_on`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/mod.rs#L40-L42) (`Handle::current().block_on`) or `block_in_place` from inside a shard worker panics immediately because each shard uses a `current_thread` runtime.
  - Any synchronous blocking inside a handler stalls every actor, timer, I/O resource, and the new-actor ingress loop (`rx.recv()`) on that shard.
- **Static round-robin placement without work stealing ([`experimental.rs:66`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L66)):**
  - Actors are permanently pinned via `next.fetch_add(1, Relaxed) % count`. Skewed actor lifetimes or skewed message rates across modulo classes can overload one shard while other shards sit idle.
- **Per-spawn env-var and mutex overhead (benchmark note):**
  - Every sharded `Actor::start()` calls `std::env::var` **three times** (`SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_SCHEDULER`, `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_BATCH`, `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_WORKERS`) and locks the global `REGISTRY` `Mutex<Weak<Pool>>` ([`actor.rs:573-577`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L573-L577), [`actor.rs:640`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L640), [`experimental.rs:95-107`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L95-L107)). In spawn-heavy benchmarks (or handlers that spawn child actors like `Nested`), this adds non-trivial process-env lock and mutex contention that default `rt::spawn` does not pay.
- **Test gating in [`full_actor_shards.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/full_actor_shards.rs#L155):**
  - Unless `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_SCHEDULER=sharded` is set in the environment, two of the four tests in `full_actor_shards.rs` early-return as no-ops and the other two run against default Tokio.

